  "reviewed_behavior": [
    "Managed fixture proof binds actual retained supervisor/stopped outcome, fixed reproducible catalog, complete CPU/vCPU/VGIC census, disk counter and one-shot HTTP confirmation. Extra vCPUs, partial/duplicate console lines and debugfs cleanup failures are covered.",
    "Typed stopped-disk custody retains the original exclusive disk flock over exact manifest/history publication; original Inspection remains stale after replacement. PID/thread, readonly descriptors, parent chains, inode and close-failure guards remain enforced.",
    "Bounded outcome/intent/completion schemas bind exact raw manifest/history/permit bytes and replay supported QMP shutdown evidence. Parsing creates no execution or checkpoint authority.",
    "Root runtime contract requires nonrecursive physical store guards, exact head transition boundaries, full completion verification and observable cleanup failures. These are integration requirements, not completed runtime evidence."
  ],
